```ts
import type { ConvexClient } from "convex/browser";
import { api } from "../../convex/_generated/api";
import type { Source } from "../../convex/research";
import type { ApparatusSettings, ProjectBrief, ResearchTarget, ResearchTargetRef } from "../types";
import { hasConfiguredAiProvider, runClientResearchExtract, runClientResearchWebSearch } from "./ai-client";
import { loadAiSettingsFromIdb, loadApparatusSettingsFromIdb } from "./idb";
import type { BibEntry } from "./bibliography";
import { loadBibliography, saveBibliography, normalizeUrl } from "./bibliography";
import { selectFreshTargets, targetKey, rankSourcesForTarget, DEFAULT_TARGETS_PER_PASS } from "./research-targets";

const DEBOUNCE_MS = 45_000;
const PASS_TTL_MS = 5 * 60_000;
const MAX_BACKGROUND_PER_FOLIO = 25;
const SNIPPET_MIN_CHARS = 40;
const MAX_TARGETS_PER_PASS = 3;
const MIN_DRAFT_CHARS = 40;
```

State track: add lastTargets, lastPassed. Keep savedThisSession etc.

`deriveQuery` removed. We keep a `brief` for prompt context but rely on clientResolve for prompt building? The extraction prompt builder currently doesn't include brief. I could add `instructions` from brief: when `startBackgroundResearch` receives a brief, we can prepend "Project context: title..." to instructions. Actually nice: pass `instructions` built once from brief. Let me compute a `briefHint` string at startBackgroundResearch:

```
const briefContext = brief ? 
  `${brief.answers.workingTitle ? `Working title: ${brief.answers.workingTitle}. ` : ""}${brief.answers.goal ? `Goal: ${brief.answers.goal}. ` : ""}${brief.answers.audience ? `Audience: ${brief.answers.audience}.` : ""}`.trim()
  : "";
```
Store `activeBriefContext`. Pass as instructions to extract.

Then runOnce:

```
async function runOnce(draftText: string) {
  if (!activeFolioId || !activeClient) return;
  const aiSettings = await loadAiSettingsFromIdb();
  if (!aiSettings || !hasConfiguredAiProvider(aiSettings)) {
    setStatus("idle");
    notify();
    return;
  }
  const trimmed = draftText.trim();
  if (trimmed.length < MIN_DRAFT_CHARS) return;

  const bib = await loadBibliography();
  const coveredKeys = new Set<string>();
  for (const e of bib) {
    if (e.folioId === activeFolioId && e.target) coveredKeys.add(e.target.kind| anchor normalized...) Actually targetKey requires anchor and kind. e.target has kind and anchor. coveredKeys.add(targetKey(e.target)).
  }
  const recentKeys = state.recentKeys (Set of targetKey strings persisted across this session).

  // dedupe via TTL to avoid runaway ~; use fingerprint of the selected query set.
  setStatus("running");
  const extract = await runClientResearchExtract({ draftText: trimmed, existingSources: writerEntries.map(e => e.title), maxTargets: MAX_TARGETS_PER_PASS, instructions: activeBriefContext }, aiSettings);
  if (!extract?.targets.length) { setStatus("idle"); return; }
  const fresh = selectFreshTargets(extract.targets, { budget: MAX_TARGETS_PER_PASS, coveredKeys, recentKeys });
  if (!fresh.length) { setStatus("idle"); return; }
  state.lastTargets = fresh;
  notify();
  const settings = await loadApparatusSettingsFromIdb();
  let saved = 0;
  for (const targetSimple of fresh) {
    const res = await searchForTarget(target, settings);
    if (!res) continue;
    const ranked = rankSourcesForTarget(res.results);
    const savedNow = await persist(target, ranked);
    saved += savedNow;
    if (savedNow > 0) recentKeys.add(targetKey(target));
  }
  state.lastQuery = fresh[0].query;
  state.lastQueryAt = Date.now();
  if (saved > 0) { state.savedThisSession += saved; notifySources(saved); }
  setStatus("idle");
}
```

searchForTarget:
```
async function searchForTarget(target, settings): Promise<{results: Source[]; provider: string} | null> {
  const query = target.query;
  const context = `In the draft, the writer writes: "${target.anchor}" — ${target.reason}`;
  const configured = await searchWithConfiguredProvider(query, context, settings);
  if (configured) return configured;
  if (activeClient) {
    const res = await activeClient.action(api.research.searchSources, { query, context });
    return res.results?.length ? { results: res.results, provider: res.provider } : null;
  }
  return null;
}
```

`searchWithConfiguredProvider` — routes by settings.researchProvider: tinyfish, model-web-search, web-mcp, hosted->null. It already returns results normalized as Source[] and provider string. For tinyfish, it uses `fetch` with query. For model-web-search: `runClientResearchWebSearch({query, context, maxResults, instructions})` — returns ClientResearchSource[]; normalize to Source? The persist uses Source shape. The existing code returns as `results: Source[]`. `runClientResearchWebSearch` returns ClientResearchSource[] which has `why`. That matches Source shape approximately (Source also has why). Good — I can make `searchModelEndpoint` return Source[] compatible.

Actually `searchWithConfiguredProvider` currently returns `{results: Source[]; provider}` for tinyfish/mcp/model with model normalized through normalizeSources which builds Source from ClientResearchSource fields (title,url,snippet,author,publisher,date,why). But `runClientResearchWebSearch` returns ClientResearchSource[], each has `why`? ClientResearchSource has `why?: string`. `normalizeSources` in background reads `rec.why`— but it receives value passed through normalizeMcpSources etc. Let me just reuse normalize for all: the model path returns ClientResearchSource[]; normalizeSources handles them.

Wait, the current `searchModelEndpoint`:
```
return runClientResearchWebSearch({...}, aiSettings);
```
which returns `{results: ClientResearchSource[], provider}` — that matches the type `{results: Source[], provider}` structurally (ClientResearchSource fields are subset/supers of Source). Fine.

Let me keep `searchWithConfiguredProvider` and the provider functions as-is (with signature (query, context, settings)) — they already take query+context. The only change: remove deriveQuery and the brief-first-280 slice logic; search provider functions unchanged. But `searchModelEndpoint` loads aiSettings itself — needs `aiSettings` param already present. It calls loadAiSettingsFromIdb() again — fine.

persist: change signature to `persistTarget(target, results)`:
```
async function persistTarget(target: ResearchTarget, ranked: Source[]): Promise<number> {
  const all = await loadBibliography();
  const seen = new Set(all.filter(e=>eo.folioId===activeFolioId).map(e=>normalizeUrl(e.url)));
  const existingBg = all.filter(e=>eo.folioId===activeFolioId && e.provenance==="background").length;
  let budget = Math.max(0, MAX_BACKGROUND_PER_FOLIO - existingBg);
  const ref: ResearchTargetRef = { kind: target.kind, anchor: target.anchor, query: target.query, reason: target.reason };
  let saved = 0;
  for (const src of ranked) {
    if (budget <=0) break;
    if (!normalizeUrl(src.url)) continue;
    if (seen.has(normalizeUrl(src.url))) continue;
    if ((src.snippet?.length ?? 0) < SNIPPET_MIN_CHARS) continue;
    const entry: BibEntry = { id: uuid, folioId, title, author, publisher, date, url, accessedAt, snippet, why: target.reason, provenance:"background", backgroundQuery: target.query, target: ref, accepted:false };
    all.push(entry); seen.add(...); saved++; budget--;
  }
  if (saved > 0) await saveBibliography(all);
  return saved;
